---
// The prose on this page is placeholder copy — rewrite it as your own. It is
// intentionally *not* in `src/i18n/`: the dictionary holds UI chrome, so a
// translator isn't handed someone else's biography, and you don't have to open
// a dictionary file to edit your own about page.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { SITE } from '../../consts';
import { t } from '../../i18n';
---

<BaseLayout
  title={t('about.title')}
  description={`About the author behind this ${SITE.title} site.`}
>
  <section class="page-head section">
    <p class="eyebrow">{t('about.eyebrow')}</p>
    <h1>A measured profile for the person behind the work.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      This page is shaped for a concise biography, a working philosophy, and the handful of details
      that help readers understand how you think.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Profile</p>
      <h2>Quiet systems, clear writing, durable interfaces.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        I work across product strategy, interface systems, and technical writing. The common thread
        is structure: making complex material easier to scan, trust, and maintain.
      </p>
      <p>
        My work focuses on performance engineering, AI systems, and low-latency computing.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label={t('about.ledgerLabel')}>
    <div class="about-ledger">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Current focus</h3>
        <p>Building fast systems, thoughtful interfaces, and durable technical documentation.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>Background</h3>
        <p>
          Experience spanning performance engineering, distributed systems, AI infrastructure, and
          technical writing.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Contact</h3>
        <p>
          Reach out through email, GitHub, or LinkedIn for collaboration and technical discussions.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Method</p>
      <h2>Structure before surface.</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        The theme treats the page like a working document: hierarchy first, rhythm second, visual
        signature third. Fine rules, generous spacing, and type contrast carry the identity without
        competing with the content.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
